# SYNOPSIS

```usage
minimal-hot image
```

# DESCRIPTION

`minimal-hot` is minimal (sdk(2)) with its frame in a hot image (hotreload(2)): the image at <image> fills the frame with a colour that moves with the frames drawn, which its state keeps.
When the file changes, the next frame runs the new image, over the same state.
With Radharc it draws in a 320x180 window; without, as in a cpu image, 320x180 pixels of its own, at 60 frames a second.

The cpu images carry it as an app, `MinimalHot`, started by the launcher's ctl (`start minimal-hot`), with the image `/data/hot/libminimalframe.so` on fs(4)'s volume.

# FILES

: `status`
  Its tree's: `image <version> loads <n> last <us> us frames <n> drawn <n>`, and `refused <why>` if the last image was refused.
: `<image>.status`
  The same, written beside the image at each load and each refusal, for a cpu session, which can't see an app's tree.

